cff-version: 1.2.0
title: driving-risk-metrics
message: >-
  If you use this software or its published evidence, please cite it using the
  metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kuo
    given-names: Tun-Yu
    alias: kuotunyu
repository-code: https://github.com/kuotunyu/driving-risk-metrics
abstract: >-
  Safety-aware evaluation for road-scene semantic segmentation. Three
  contemporary models are trained on BDD100K under one frozen protocol with three
  seeds each and evaluated once on a locked cohort. The study reports
  instance-balanced coverage, risk-weighted cost, confidence calibration and
  paired bootstrap intervals, and finds that the paired interval for the two best
  models includes zero on mean IoU while excluding zero on recall over the
  vulnerable-road-user classes. Every published number is bound to a committed
  artifact by a claims registry that fails the build if it cannot be reproduced.
keywords:
  - semantic-segmentation
  - autonomous-driving
  - model-evaluation
  - calibration
  - reproducibility
  - bdd100k
